      "expected_answerable": true,
      "result": {
        "status": "answered",
        "answer": "For a binary label \\(y\\in\\{0,1\\}\\), logistic regression predicts \\(\\hat y=\\sigma(w\\cdot x+b)\\). The Bernoulli likelihood is \\(P(y\\mid x)=\\hat y^y(1-\\hat y)^{1-y}\\). Taking its negative log gives the binary cross-entropy loss:\n\\[\nL_{\\mathrm{CE}}(\\hat y,y)=-\\bigl[y\\log\\hat y+(1-y)\\log(1-\\hat y)\\bigr].\n\\]\nSubstituting the logistic prediction:\n\\[\nL_{\\mathrm{CE}}=-\\bigl[y\\log\\sigma(w\\cdot x+b)+(1-y)\\log(1-\\sigma(w\\cdot x+b))\\bigr].\n\\]",
